<<~ ahu slot=`#/entry`>>

! The Landmark Map ~ M4 walked backwards

The forward road (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/milestones`>>) walks from the span toward the landmarks. This carrier walks the other way: it stands at `M4`, reads what the code demands for the rite to succeed, and recurses back until it reaches code that stands today (operator, 2026-11-07: //"the shortest path from M4 to here (walking it backwards)"//).

''Provenance.'' A Sol reader seat (`Backwalker`, `gpt-6.1-sol` high, read-only) read the road as `_0`, presence acknowledged and essence unclaimed, then read the code at span head `e1d801042`. Lares-Awakens re-measured three load-bearing claims against source (the compound rite's step test, L24's renewal writer, L23's tombstone source); all three held. Every size, order and "clear" step below carries the seat's INFER mark: testimony from a read, never a run. The seat's full hand-back, with every file:line citation, rests at `~/.lares-scratch/reverse-walk/seats/sol-1/final.md`. The canon pass at span head `e44da0167`, trued to `0179899a8`, re-measured the links its lands moved (5, 6, 7 and 12) against source and git, and the road took the trues this read named; the map reads the code as it stands at `0179899a8`.

''How to read it.'' `STANDS` means the source exists and reaches the traced path, with no claim of a passing run. `ON-PATH` means the rite's code cannot succeed without the row. `OFF-PATH†` means the rite's code never calls it, while the road still owes it before the rite: OFF-PATH waives no obligation. The map tells the controller which rows the code itself forces and which the road's law adds; the road's law still governs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-dogfood-stand`>>

!! The near landmark ~ the dogfood stand

The operator split the hearth in two (2026-11-07: //"Pono, approve the dogfood/keeper split."//; <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings`>>). The DOGFOOD hearth stands early from the same primitives the shortest mechanical route reuses (#/m4-in-code), re-standable as often as the house needs, so the house works from a live Lararium; `M5` builds on it as the spine. The KEEPER rite stays `M4` below, and every qualification the backward walk names still binds it.

''The proof set'' (lane `dogfood-proof`, landed, PR #204; existing suites first, one entry point `pnpm test:e2e:dogfood`, one CI shard): the stand through the kahua founding stage (`kahua-founding-stage`); memory surviving a content-keyed re-stand (`dogfood-memory-restand`, with `L9`'s `stageRowTitle`, so a re-pour after a re-found lands the same tiddlers); the MCP seat's write reaching its projected file (`mcp-seat-binds-the-hearth`); the outbound bridge on journal events; and the container's compose root, shim and founding-seat tests.

''The route.''
# ''Ready state.'' Every gate lane lands and the span reads green; a full `pnpm build` and the product image at the landed head follow (`GIT_REV=$(git rev-parse HEAD) docker compose -f docker-compose.surface.yml build lares`, its `org.opencontainers.image.revision` read back); then a check reads the live Lararium launching containerized, web3 and local-first.
# ''Homes.'' The house root rests outside every checkout and stays kept across re-stands (`LARES_HOUSE`, bound at `/lar`: hearth, projections, library and config); the workspace names the main repo (`LARES_WORKSPACE`), where live wiki and canon writes land as source-control write-back. A re-founding clears the hearth alone; a re-stand renames an old house root aside, never deletes it, and memory re-pours by content key.
# ''The stand'', by the operator's hands on an attached TTY: `tools/lares-container.sh found --hearth --name '<label>' --chair '<chair>'` (the route and the cold-key card read-back on paper; `found --hearth` founds persona zero whole), then `up` (the live unlock), `vessel seed --apply --yes`, `vessel read`, `persona list --json`, `nexus seal show`, `meme list --recipe default --json`.
# ''Read-backs.'' `<state>/wikis/kahua-<tag>` and `<state>/bags/kahua-<tag>` stand, and no `bags/daemon` stands anywhere; the `lares` MCP seat connects to the standing daemon, and `meme_put` then `meme_get` round-trips one tiddler whose file lands in the projection.
# ''Then `M5`'': `L17`'s full TW5 caps on the MCP seat, `L8`, `L10`, `L11`, `L18`, `L19` (once lane `kapae-disk`, PR #205, lands a burned row's kāpae on disk and back) and `L13`; then the harness moves into the Lararium (its controls as signed daemon-wiki tiddlers), and only then any measurement work.

''What the dogfood stand skips, and the keeper rite keeps'': `P27` (parked: its head reds real boots in CI, so the old deciders stand), the rest of `M6`, browser slices 6 and 7, `X0b`, the joined gate, the phone walk and the final bake. None of them gates the dogfood hearth; each still gates `M4`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/m4-in-code`>>

!! M4 as the code defines it

Three different boundaries answer to "the hearth stands":

# ''The offline hearth act.'' `lares vessel found --hearth --name '<label>'` (`lares-cli/src/commands/found.ts`, then `lararium-node/src/commands/found-hearth.ts`) initializes the place, seats the one-chair seed charter, founds persona zero, admits its group and lands the Kahu realm. It prints "the hearth stands" before any daemon starts.
# ''The compound rite.'' `lares vessel rite founding` (`lares-cli/src/commands/vessel.ts`, `runFoundingRite`) runs found, stand, seed. It passes no `--hearth` and calls no unlock, and it halts only on a nonzero exit, while `stand` returns zero on an `ok: false` payload unless the host refuses. A failed stand therefore flows on into seed.
# ''The live, sovereign, seeded household under the operator's hand.'' The founding runbook (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook`>>) runs `found --hearth`, `up` (a TTY unlock), then `vessel seed --apply --yes`. No call inside the rite demands household HTTPS, a phone, the joined gate or `M6`; the road demands them before the operator's `M4`.

''The shortest mechanical route'' reuses the separate primitives the runbook already names. ''The shortest authorized route'' finishes the road's pre-rite qualifications, proves the final candidate in a scratch household, then hands the operator those same primitives on a TTY. The code enforces only part of the road's admission rule.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-backward-walk`>>

!! The backward walk

A dependency graph, not one serial train: links 3 to 7 branch independently.

|! # |! Precondition |! State |! The smallest change that clears it |
| 1 | The operator's qualified M4 hand-off | UNWIRED as an executable gate | gather the road's receipts against the final candidate; keep the operator's TTY act; no new product gate follows of necessity |
| 2 | A joined household over trusted HTTPS, with a real phone | UNWIRED as a proved gate | browser admission, custody and lift already compose; HTTPS surfaces refuse by name; a LAN-HTTP phone meets `insecure-origin`; the browser weld's W5 reports an unwired disk leg (that leg belongs to `L4p`, never this gate). Clear: links 3 to 7, then a scratch node, browser and real-phone founding and join on the final image |
| 3 | Browser founding and retry idempotence (slice 6, `X0b`) | UNWIRED across the sequence | ceremony, atom, archive and anchor persist before bootstrap lands in `loadGenesis`, with no single commit spanning them; carry a durable founding-operation identity across the cut points; prove one atom, one group, no orphan rows |
| 4 | Durability disclosure before binding (slice 7) | UNWIRED | the page reads durability only after the vessel stands live, and swallows an unreadable store; read and show it before founding or joining binds; settle partial-keystore loss apart from whole-origin loss |
| 5 | `P27` at four crossings | PARKED; its composer STANDS | `capTierShareDecision` and the contract secrets registry still hold no production caller on the span, and the four crossings keep their old deciders; lane `p27-wire` (PR #200) wired them on the standing 5b under the seat's leaf ruling (the secrets plane node-only, a browser leaf flooring it by established absence), and its head reds real boots in CI (the manifest handler's `DeclaredTierRefusal`, a browser `house` TypeError, the own-hearth canon pin, the persona-ring admit, the isomorphic hull) while its unit and composition suites read green. Clear: a booted-vessel witness first (a real boot that mounts its islands with no manifest refusal), red on the lane head, then the cures; invent no secrets store to give the registry a caller |
| 6 | The named security dispositions | mixed | `L23` LANDED (PR #201: a drop lands as a device-signed act on the face-private board outside every custody write, bound to its ledger owner, and the board's change history keeps it; its named limits ride the road's `L31`); `L24`'s writer STANDS (`device-admit.ts` appends the renewed `device-edge`; re-measure its scope, never rebuild); `L25`/`L26` residues UNWIRED; `L27` base STANDS, two residual witnesses owed; `L29` base STANDS, tails need measurement; `K22`/`L28` reviews owed after `M6`; `K23` retirement STANDS |
| 7 | `M6` before the rite | slices 1 and 2 STAND; the end state UNWIRED | slice 2 (PR #203) surfaces a forked founder lineage before unknown standing, never caches an aside, never seats an overtaken proof, refuses tampering on the epoch-free founder edge, wakes the seat on both shores from the fleet board's lift, and asks ingest's guard at the mutating call; live lease readers still fold signed epochs, `persona lease` still rolls one, browser founding still writes `leaseEpoch: 0`, and genesis keeps the `lararium-genesis-seed/v1` literal. Clear (slices 3 and 4, after the dogfood stand): slice 2's owed rows with the census that refuses an incomplete view, retire lease authority, burn its writers, change the literal in the one final bake |
| 8 | Seeding under a lit, unlocked face | STANDS as primitives; BROKEN in the compound rite | the compound neither founds a hearth nor unlocks before seed; use found `--hearth`, start, live unlock, seed; read Kahu projection as its own receipt |
| 9 | A live sovereign daemon | STANDS; compound success propagation BROKEN | each boot starts with empty custody and unlock recomposes; `stand` can read `ok: false` and exit zero; the container's `vessel rite` routes into the CLI without the host shim's unlock; keep the host `up` path and verify held custody and sovereign standing |
| 10 | Seed charter, persona zero, custody, card readback | STANDS | `found --hearth` does it whole; bare `found` founds a faceless place and `persona new 0` then refuses; the act needs a TTY, a label and the place and chair card readbacks |
| 11 | Fresh roots, usable genesis, runnable artifacts | STANDS conditionally; final qualification UNWIRED | founding refuses occupied storage (`OccupiedStoreRefusal`); Docker copies committed genesis and never bakes; a missing seed pin permits an unpinned boot; one final bake and image build, then check revision, genesis, artifacts and mounts together |
| 12 | Today's code and instruments | STANDS; green unread | shared composition, TTY custody, charter founding, floor boot, unlock, seed, browser lift, HTTPS profiles, the store wall's refusals and the broker's claim and door bounds all stand at this head; the exact candidate's CI and held-out receipts settle green |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-shortest-path`>>

!! The shortest path forward

The walk reversed into slices. Sizes and order carry INFER; the road's four-lane ceiling and one owner per compose hunk still hold. The dogfood stand (#/the-dogfood-stand) runs first and reuses slice S's foundation; the slices below walk the keeper rite after it.

# ''S · Reuse the standing foundation'' (links 12 to 8). Keep 5b, custody, charter founding, unlock, seed and the HTTPS machinery; rebuild nothing an older road inventory calls absent. HTTPS, DNS and certificate preparation start alongside.
# ''L · Finish `M6`'' (link 7). Slices 3 and 4: slice 2's owed rows, the dyad census with incomplete-view refusal, the lease burn, the format literal. Parallel with the security slice on disjoint files.
# ''L · Close the security dispositions'' (link 6). Re-measure `L24`; finish `L25`/`L26`; measure `L27`'s and `L29`'s residuals; review `K22`/`L28` under `M6`'s shape.
# ''L · Wire `P27` at four crossings'' (link 5). On the standing 5b, from lane `p27-wire`'s parked work, behind a booted-vessel witness; serialize shared compose edits.
# ''L · Browser slices 6 and 7, then `X0b`'' (links 3 and 4), after `P27` in the road's order.
# ''M · Bake and build the final candidate'' (link 11).
# ''M/L · Prove `M3` from that candidate'' (link 2): joined node and browser founding, `X0b`'s crash controls, `G55`, `G56`, drain checks, the real phone over household HTTPS, durability before binding, green CI and held-out on the exact SHA.
# ''S · Pre-rite and `M4` by hand'' (links 1, 9 to 11): confirm projection, rename old homes, then on the TTY `found --hearth`, `up` with its live unlock, `vessel seed --apply --yes`, and the read-backs (`vessel read`, `persona list`, `nexus seal show`, `meme list --recipe default`); then the browser slot and the join acts.

''Keep the compound rite off the critical path.'' The runbook's manual route supplies the orchestration the compound lacks. Its false success on a failed stand and its misleading help stand as one bounded defect to cure if the house keeps advertising it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/rows-sorted`>>

!! Roadmap rows sorted by the code's own demand

* ''ON-PATH'' (the rite's code needs it): 5b; `M6`'s landed lineage readers; usable artifacts, roots and origin projection; fresh empty storage; TTY custody and cards; valid genesis; `found --hearth`; live unlock; seed; `L1`, `L2`, `L5`, `L7`; the `L22`/`S1`–`S3b` ward and tag model; the `L29` drain foundation.
* ''OFF-PATH†'' (the code never calls it; the road still owes it before the rite): every `M0` and `M1` row (train and instrument law); `P27`; slices 6 and 7; `X0b`; `K22`; `L28`; `K23` (already retired); the `M6` timeout sweep, version burn, dyad census and lease burn; the `M3` joined gate and phone walk; the final rebuild; the browser passphrase slot and fleet join acts; `L24` to `L26`; `G55`.
* ''UNCLEAR'' (a measurement settles it): `L27`'s residual projection witness (seed's real Kahu-gated receipt); `L29`'s tails (dedicated-worker pagehide, herm drain); `G56` (dial order against the joined gate); `F11` (if agent writes enter `M4` acceptance); `L16` (a cold corpus without `.git`).
* ''OFF-PATH, after the keeper rite by the road's own word'' (every `M5` row builds first on the dogfood hearth): `L3`/`home tend`, `L15`, `L4p`/`L4f` and every `M5` row, `S4`–`S6`, the mirror, harness and AI-harness tails, `M7`, `M8`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/collisions`>>

!! Canon against code ~ the trues still open

Each row names a place where the house's word and the source still disagree. The road took the rest of this read's trues (the store wall's land, `L24`'s writer, `OccupiedStoreRefusal`, the socket-cutover inventories, the `.env` bleed).

# ''The CLI help'' advertises bare `rite founding` then `persona new 0`; bare `found` seats no charter and persona zero refuses without one. The runbook's `found --hearth` holds; the help and the runbook's separate `persona new 0` line owe their true (the road's pre-rite).
# ''The compound rite's comment'' promises a halt at the first refusing step; `stand` exits zero on most failed payloads, so a failed stand flows into seed (one bounded build lane, if the house keeps advertising the compound).
# ''The compound rite's commentary'' explains boot class by an env passphrase; boot now starts without custody and the TTY reaches the live custody frame.
# ''"The hearth stands"'' printed by `found` reads as no `M4` qualification; it prints before the vessel stands.
# ''`K22` against `M7`'' — `K22` proposes wiring a helper that reconstructs a root; `M7` rotates without reconstruction. A critical review settles it before any wire.
# ''The test re-cut's place'' — one road passage sets it before founding, the operator-order passage after standing; prefer the explicit order.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/unsettled`>>

!! What the read could not settle

Each needs a run, never another read: exact-candidate green (CI and held-out on the final SHA); artifact freshness after the final bake; `M6` completeness under injected missing lineage, stale replicas and incomplete frontiers; browser crash behavior at each persistence cut; erasure on real phones, keystore-only against whole-origin; `L24`'s full scope over every lease-advancing act; `L27`/`L29` residuals and `G56`; household HTTPS and DNS on the actual phone; a kill between init and seed-pin persistence (the pin carries no atomic guarantee today); and a recorded scratch-household qualification of the final candidate before the operator's live re-found.

<<~/ahu>>

